.TH SIGROK\-FWEXTRACT\-INTRONIX\-LOGICPORT 1 "October 18, 2026"
.SH "NAME"
sigrok\-fwextract\-intronix\-logicport \- Get Intronix LogicPort bitstreams
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B sigrok\-fwextract\-intronix\-logicport [\-o DIR] FILE
.br
.B sigrok\-fwextract\-intronix\-logicport [\-o DIR] \-d
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
This tool provides the FPGA bitstream file for the Intronix LogicPort
LA1034 USB logic analyzer. The FPGA is volatile and gets configured by the
libsigrok driver with one of eight bitstreams, depending on the sampling
mode (timing SDR, timing DDR at 500MHz, and several state mode variants).
.PP
All eight bitstreams ship in one file called "LogicPort.ccf", inside the
vendor's Windows installer [1]. The libsigrok driver uses this file as is,
under the name intronix\-logicport.ccf. The tool takes either LogicPort.ccf
(from an installed copy of the software) or the installer itself, or it can
download the installer. It checks the file and saves it unmodified.
Unpacking the installer needs 7\-Zip (7zz, 7z or 7za), as the file is
Deflate64 compressed. To download the installer and get the file, run:
.PP
.B "  $ sigrok-fwextract-intronix-logicport -d"
.br
.RB "  Downloading https://www.pctestinstruments.com/downloads/logicport_2371.exe"
.br
.RB "  saved 8387769 bytes to intronix-logicport.ccf (sha256 9298a5ea...)"
.PP
The output above is for LogicPort software build 2371. Copy the resulting
file to the location where libsigrok expects to find firmware files.
By default this is /usr/local/share/sigrok\-firmware.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-download
Download the vendor installer [1] instead of reading FILE.
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-output\-dir DIR
Write the files to DIR instead of the current directory.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
Exits with 0 on success, 1 on most failures.
